# What was built: one artifact per composition, and nothing else.
/build/

# How it was built — the generated C++, the build system, and what the toolchain left
# behind. Written in full on every run, and never worth keeping.
/.bareruby/
/dump/

# The SDKs and toolchains a build reaches for, downloaded or built in place. Other
# people's releases, and this desk's copy of them.
/.tools/

# config/target.yml is deliberately not listed. Which compositions this project is built
# for is true of the project, and belongs with it. What is true of one desk — the serials
# under `boards:`, the paths under `options:` — sits inside those same entries, and moves
# out of this file on the day a second desk needs it to.
